  "statement": "Given an integer array `nums`, return _the number of triplets chosen from the array that can make triangles if we take them as side lengths of a triangle_.\n\n**Example 1:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [2,2,3,4]\nOutput: 3\nExplanation: Valid combinations are: \n2,3,4 (using the first 2)\n2,3,4 (using the second 2)\n2,2,3\n```\n\n**Example 2:**\n\n```\nInput: nums = [4,2,3,4]\nOutput: 4\n```\n\n**Constraints:**\n\n*   `1 <= nums.length <= 1000`\n*   `0 <= nums[i] <= 1000`",
  "constraints": [
    "1 <= nums.length <= 1000",
    "0 <= nums[i] <= 1000"
  ],
